title: "EXO-SOMATIC Cognition: A Framework for Substrate-Independent Cognitive Systems"
authors:
  - family-names: "Trubnikov"
    given-names: "Dima"
version: "2.0"
date-released: "2026-06-11"
url: "https://github.com/trubnikov/Exo-Somatic"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.20636329"
license: "CC-BY-4.0"
abstract: >
  A framework for cognitive systems that exist as information patterns rather than
  being bound to fixed physical devices: operational criteria for substrate
  independence, falsifiability conditions, resonance-based memory, branching
  identity, and a completed substrate-transition experiment (Ocean -> Hermes Agent,
  2026) with cryptographically verifiable identity via SES Partitura serialization.
keywords:
  - substrate independence
  - cognitive architecture
  - persistent identity
  - agent serialization
  - verifiable identity
